{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go","id":1268002,"title":"Should the use of \"NuWW\" go?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-16T13:08:24-08:00","id":1268002,"title":"Should the use of \"NuWW\" go?","content":"I would like to have a discussion, one which is bothering me of late. Should the use of terms like NuWW go? I have heard allot of terminology thrown about on these forums that seem to be purposefully spreading hate. I could be wrong, but the more I see it the more I get mad as it seems to be driven by a need to divide and marginalize. I personally feel marginalized by it. That because I like the direction that WW has taken and when I see someone use NuWW when they could have just said WW I fell like I am being viewed by association as something evil or a part of the problem. When people use speech to separate they create an us verses them mentality. Many times that wording could be avoided all together.<br /> <br /> You don't need to say NuWW or Paradox wolf and such. You can just say WW. To me the use is similar to things like obamacare or trumpcare or whatever. They are meant to judge, lump-in, marginalize, and trivialize groups of people or ideals bundle them up with all sorts of emotions into a single word and they are not helpful, they are in essence spiteful and a form of passive aggressiveness that is used to attack and stifle not inform or grow.<br /> <br /> You can just say WW, people are intelligent enough to understand who you are talking about.<br /> <br /> I short I think that people should respect one another and this does not seem respectful to people in my mind and you can say you don't like something without using this kind of speech.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T13:51:10-08:00","id":1268026,"title":"","content":"I think its still useful because a lot of folks still don't seem to understand that the WW owned by Paradox is a completely different company than the one that was running and taken over by CCP. There are still many, many people who think that because pre-CCP WW did something it has indicators for Paradox owned WW when there is very little creative DNA shared by the two.<br /> <br /> I can stop using NuWW and start using Parawolf or Paradox-owned-WW though if that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T15:14:12-08:00","id":1268057,"title":"","content":"And it also could just be me eye-twitching for no good reason. Shrug. I just didn't think that the differentiation needed to be made and some of the posts where it was used seemed to be unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Or when I first heard it it was used it was used in a negative fashion and it has colored my perspective of its use from that point forward. I just figured I would get other peoples take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T15:28:31-08:00","id":1268060,"title":"","content":"I like Parawolf myself, but, really, it's common use what defines what words come and go and their meaning in the end. And I don't think it's such a slur as to be banned from polite conversation (then again I don't think that of SJW either, but this forums thinks different. You're free of making your case).<br /> <br /> Perhaps you should appropriate of the therm NuWW instead, using it in a positive fashions?. That sure worked for football teams where I come from","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T15:37:32-08:00","id":1268067,"title":"","content":"I use it because it is literally the &quot;new&quot; White Wolf, with absolutely no ties to the previous White Wolf Game Studio other than owning the IP produced by that entity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T16:36:50-08:00","id":1268094,"title":"","content":"Also, using WWGS (White Wolf Game Studio) and WWEAB (White Wolf Entertainment Aktiebolag) to separate them would be really confusing to people that don't know the letters beyond WW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T17:11:55-08:00","id":1268104,"title":"","content":"Considering all the difficulty Onyx Path has had distinguishing itself from White Wolf over the last two decades, I think it's wasted effort to try to establish some label distinction between White Wolf v1 and White Wolf v2 (or is it v3?). No matter who owns the company or who runs it, White Wolf is White Wolf. That's the point of companies buying and keeping a brand. You can clearly make a distinction about White Wolf in the 90s, 00s, and recently, but special terminology like &quot;nuWW&quot; is just Internet communities making their own inclusive lingo. That's my take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T17:25:43-08:00","id":1268108,"title":"","content":"A company with no shared personnel and a decade gap from the previous iteration absolutely deserves a new name.<br /> <br /> How the heck is it \u201cmarginalizing\u201d you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T20:20:08-08:00","id":1268142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1268108#post1268108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A company with no shared personnel and a decade gap from the previous iteration absolutely deserves a new name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then there are many countries, organizations, clubs, companies, political parties, religions, and so forth that should change their names. Just because the founders of something are no longer present does not necessitate a name change or the need to separate them from their founding unless you feel that they strayed from their founding philosophies in which case it is being used to divide them. So my question still stands why is this different? Why do we need to divide them? is this a way to just be passive aggressive towards something that is not liked?<br /> <br /> It seems to me that people feel the need to differentiate but I wonder why? It seems to me that those using the terminology see a difference in the two and feel that they need to make the distinction so that others do not see the two as the same. This to me shows a need to make a separation rather than a need for a clarification because you could just use WW and the meaning would be known to those who know there is a difference and to those who didn't know it would not matter. The only time it would matter is if WW was being made out to be a bad thing and then the clarification is once again there to show separation so that those individuals who do not know the difference will not think that WW has always been this way. This once again is coming from a need to separate the two and clarification is just a justification for its use after the fact.<br /> <br /> I am certain it is a combination of both those who truly wish to be accurate and those who are passively attacking WW. This to me says that such divisive terminology should not be used as it enables those who just wish to spew hate in much the same but to a more extreme manor that certain extremists would place certain key phrases within texts and anyone that used that same terminology would be lumped in with those extremists even if they did not mean it in such a manor. <br /> <br /> Not only have I seen it used but I have also seen it not used by the same people which makes it seem that clarification is not necessarily the motivation of its use in all cases.<br /> <br /> It seems a common thing to use terms to a similar albeit greater extreme. Wether you use terms like republican, democrat, alt-right, leftist, christian, white, socialist, the list goes on and on but they all can be used to accurately describe a person or group of people but they can also be used in a passive aggressive or flat out disrespectful manor and some have been used so much as a negative connotation that they are no longer used as an accurate description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1268108#post1268108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the heck is it &quot;marginalizing&quot; you?</div> </div> </div> </div>When use of such terminology seems to be used interchangeably by individuals, except when they are displeased It makes it hard for me to see its use as anything other than an attempt to disrespect, marginalize, or passively be aggressive towards WW. <br /> <br /> Have you ever had a thought that would be associated with a group even though you do not espouse the whole of their dogma only to be lumped in with that group and all of the negative connotations that go with it? If not you are lucky but this is a common occurrence in todays society. <br /> <br /> Every individual is a complex grouping of thoughts and beliefs that can not be easily summed up by a single thought. but yet we try to create words that incapsulate that and place those individuals in these boxes so we can parse information and make decisions quickly. This is how our brains work. We also take individuals and associate them with similar constructs so to say someone likes trump your brain has already made leaps on the person that he is based on that statement for the good or ill of that individual. So the word Trump and all of its connotations in your brain can marginalize or exalt an individual that you associate with him in your mind.<br /> <br /> The same can be said if you are using a term such as &quot;NuWW&quot; to marginalize a company or to categorize it as bad you would also trivialize individuals who you have connected to it as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T20:33:45-08:00","id":1268145,"title":"","content":"Sort of a moot point, with nuWW dead, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T20:45:27-08:00","id":1268148,"title":"","content":"Yes since WW is now just PI. Like nWoD became CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T21:01:21-08:00","id":1268152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moogle001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1268104#post1268104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering all the difficulty Onyx Path has had distinguishing itself from White Wolf over the last two decades,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... you realize Onyx Path is only 7 years old, right? From 2004 - 2011 (two decades is pushing things a lot here) the original WW had merged/was bought by CCP and operated as a sub-imprint of CCP.<br /> <br /> You're conflating the time when WW was owned by CCP with Onyx Path's existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No matter who owns the company or who runs it, White Wolf is White Wolf. </div> </div> </div>But they're not? The original WW was a full game studio that developed and published TT games, eventually even licensing their properties for things beyond their in-house skills. Paradox's White Wolf subsidiary has the primary focus of licensing properties rather than publishing TT RPG products.<br /> <br /> So, even past anything such as content, or political stances, or personalities, or whatever, their goals as companies is actually different. The old WW's primary function was to make TT RPGs. The new WW's primary function is to license WoD/CofD/Exalted IPs to people to make products with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the point of companies buying and keeping a brand. </div> </div> </div>No, the point of buying and maintaining a brand is to use brand loyalty to keep existing customers to profit off the brand. Disney didn't buy Lucasfilm to keep Lucasfilm operating exactly the same with a new owner, it bought Lucasfilm because the Star Wars brand prints money and it came with a few other decent things to profit from too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can clearly make a distinction about White Wolf in the 90s, 00s, and recently, but special terminology like &quot;nuWW&quot; is just Internet communities making their own inclusive lingo. That's my take. </div> </div> </div>This take bugs me, because I've only seen it used to cast aspersions on parts of the WoD fandom.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't like what the new White Wolf is doing for these reasons.&quot;<br /> &quot;Why are you calling it 'new?' It's just White Wolf, why are you trying to create divides?&quot;<br /> <br /> And thus the reasons and actual discussions about things are ignored, and lines are drawn by the people proclaiming they don't want division within the fandom; derailing the conversation to be about names instead of any actual issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:58:33-08:00","id":1268180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1268152#post1268152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um... you realize Onyx Path is only 7 years old, right? From 2004 - 2011 (two decades is pushing things a lot here) the original WW had merged/was bought by CCP and operated as a sub-imprint of CCP.<br /> <br /> You're conflating the time when WW was owned by CCP with Onyx Path's existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very easily could be. Kinda reinforces my point, doesn't it? It's very hard to keep these corporate distinctions apart. I consider myself an avid WW/OP fan, but the years blend. I feel like I've been explaining to friends that OP is not WW for so long it must be two decades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1268152#post1268152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they're not? The original WW was a full game studio that developed and published TT games, eventually even licensing their properties for things beyond their in-house skills. Paradox's White Wolf subsidiary has the primary focus of licensing properties rather than publishing TT RPG products.<br /> <br /> So, even past anything such as content, or political stances, or personalities, or whatever, their goals as companies is actually different. The old WW's primary function was to make TT RPGs. The new WW's primary function is to license WoD/CofD/Exalted IPs to people to make products with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, the point of buying and maintaining a brand is to use brand loyalty to keep existing customers to profit off the brand. Disney didn't buy Lucasfilm to keep Lucasfilm operating exactly the same with a new owner, it bought Lucasfilm because the Star Wars brand prints money and it came with a few other decent things to profit from too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my point. I'm not asserting anything you're saying about the new WW is incorrect. I'm stating that the WW brand is much stronger than any of these details, and that's why it's stuck around across several purchases. Of the super niche of TTRPG players that is WoD fans, only a small percentage have followed WW's corporate history. So I personally think most fans will be confused by the term &quot;nuWW&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1268152#post1268152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This take bugs me, because I've only seen it used to cast aspersions on parts of the WoD fandom.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't like what the new White Wolf is doing for these reasons.&quot;<br /> &quot;Why are you calling it 'new?' It's just White Wolf, why are you trying to create divides?&quot;<br /> <br /> And thus the reasons and actual discussions about things are ignored, and lines are drawn by the people proclaiming they don't want division within the fandom; derailing the conversation to be about names instead of any actual issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's literally the opposite of what I intend, but please forgive me as this thread is about terminology rather than issues. In the same way that I found referring to a certain individual as &quot;Dracula&quot; confusing at first, it was unclear to me at first why people we're using the term &quot;nuWW&quot;. And thus far it seems to be used as deragatory, which as a longtime WW/OP fan I find incredibly unfortunate. But my point is, Internet communities make up special terminology and it mostly serves to exclude those who are not part of that community's current consensus. So while I don't care that strongly about it, if I was asked to vote I'd stand with just WW.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T05:08:03-08:00","id":1268229,"title":"","content":"The term 'nuWW' isn't 'marginalising' anyone. Even if you see it as an attack, that's not the same thing as 'marginalising'. You can be attacked even if you're not on the margins of society (see: Trump, Theresa May, just about any famous/high-profile person ever).<br /> <br /> No one is rounding V5 players up in camps or attacking them for trying to use the bathroom or denying them their civil liberties because of the term 'nuWW'. <br /> <br /> (Though, as I say this, I know a few people in Russia and Chechnya might be in actual trouble right now, but it's not because nuWW is an at-risk minority group. It's because nuWW published some material that put people at risk.)<br /> <br /> In fact, if anything, it's 'nuWW' itself that has potentially created problems for marginalised people. It's not the term itself causing problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T08:14:06-08:00","id":1268278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1268229#post1268229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term 'nuWW' isn't 'marginalising' anyone. Even if you see it as an attack, that's not the same thing as 'marginalising'. You can be attacked even if you're not on the margins of society (see: Trump, Theresa May, just about any famous/high-profile person ever).<br /> <br /> No one is rounding V5 players up in camps or attacking them for trying to use the bathroom or denying them their civil liberties because of the term 'nuWW'.<br /> <br /> (Though, as I say this, I know a few people in Russia and Chechnya might be in actual trouble right now, but it's not because nuWW is an at-risk minority group. It's because nuWW published some material that put people at risk.)<br /> <br /> In fact, if anything, it's 'nuWW' itself that has potentially created problems for marginalised people. It's not the term itself causing problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry? <br /> <br /> Marginalized - <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">treat (a person, group, or concept) as insignificant or peripheral.<br /> <br /> Literally what you seemingly did in your first sentence. It has nothing to do with actual actions of causing physical suffering. It is actions or wording that make others feel insignificant. By making a term that is </span></span>dismissive<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> you marginalize groups of individuals that you lump in with that term or that are lumped in with the group you have used the term to </span></span>describe<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">.<br /> <br /> This has nothing to do with what WW did. What WW did was wrong and they are making steps to not do it again in the future. I am not saying correct it as I don't think that is possible. This is about what some people here, you being the example, continue to do without correction.<br /> <br /> Please notice I didn't need to use a new term to describe WW or my displeasure with their actions. So since clarity was not what was needed I can only conclude that its use is one of spitefulness and </span></span>hypocrisy<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">.</span></span><br /> <br /> hypocrisy- <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">the practice of claiming to have moral standards or beliefs to which one's own behavior does not conform; pretense.<br /> <br /> I am guilty of hypocrisy on many </span></span>occasions<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> but I try to correct it within myself whenever I see it rear it ugly head. The use of a terminology that is being used to marginalize or the disrespectful attitude toward others in the same breath as criticizing their actions for the same thing is an example of this. Much like I am doing to you now. I am lecturing you on morals while at the same time taking a moral high ground. The manor in which I am doing it could be seen as </span></span>disrespectful<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> even though I feel I am trying to be respectful in my approach and probably failing so I will try to correct this and move on.<br /> <br /> The point of this discussion was to see if what I was feeling was from something i</span></span>ntentional<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> or not and to have a discussion on whether or not a correction should be made to the way we speak to each other. As it has been pointed out WW is no more so it is somewhat a moot point, but unfortunately many still persist in using terminology that is now incorrect. So once again I can only conclude that its use is an attempt to marginalize or just be spiteful especially by continuing to use it. It is not being used in many instances for clarification.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T13:17:47-08:00","id":1268382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moogle001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1268180#post1268180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I very easily could be. Kinda reinforces my point, doesn't it? It's very hard to keep these corporate distinctions apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>And calling any terminology to separate them &quot;divisive&quot; makes this worse, not better. Having shorthand for which version of WW we're talking about is actually useful because the last 15 years have been pretty confusing and calling it all WW makes it worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I personally think most fans will be confused by the term &quot;nuWW&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Sure. But then they ask, and people can explain that WW was bought by a different company to explain why whatever they're talking about justifies differentiating. You might have noticed that I don't always use nWW or whatever. I don't like 'nuWW' because the u annoys me on a purely personal aesthetic level (developed from the use of nu-metal as a heavy metal subgenre).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well that's literally the opposite of what I intend, but please forgive me as this thread is about terminology rather than issues. </div> </div> </div>And... being divisive among the fanbase is generally the opposite of the intentions of people that chose to differentiate between old and new WW when they do so. Reading &quot;nuWW&quot; as an attack is, IME, not paying any attention to the intentions of the people talking.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is a thread about terminology, I was illustrating how this is used as I've seen it: to accuse others of being divisive to disguise truly divisive actions (intent being whatever it is).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But my point is, Internet communities make up special terminology and it mostly serves to exclude those who are not part of that community's current consensus. </div> </div> </div>Subcultural slang and lingo is a few thousand years older than the Internet. Human do it pretty much automatically. It is not rooted in the intention to exclude others, but to reference internal shared experiences. This can be intimidating to outsides and create feelings of exclusion, but rarely is it done for that purpose. The few times it's used for exclusionary purposes, it's generally by minorities seeking to protect themselves from majority cultures hostile to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1268278#post1268278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marginalized - <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">treat (a person, group, or concept) as insignificant or peripheral.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">And... who's treating nWW or its fans as insignificant or peripheral? Nobody's complaining loudly about them because they think the company doesn't matter to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By making a term that is </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> dismissive<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> you marginalize groups of individuals that you lump in with that term or that are lumped in with the group you have used the term to </span></span>describe<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">1) You're proclaiming the term as dismissive without actual back up of this. &quot;I prefer oWW to nWW&quot; is dismissive in what way? The fact that there are people dismissive of nWW that also use the shorthand doesn't prove the shorthand itself is dismissive.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;I think Mitch McConnell is a ineffective sham of a Republican that can only get his way by cheating the system and selling out Republic ideals.&quot; is pretty dismissive of him, but how have I marginalized him? How have I even marginalized Republicans?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is about what some people here, you being the example, continue to do without correction. </div> </div> </div>So, what you're saying is calling for people to stop using terms like nWW or nuWW is explicitly to police the language of the boards to correct the indisputable fact that disliking V5 openly is wrong, and such people need to feel dismissed for their insignificant grognard howling so that they either come around by social pressure or flee the community.<br /> <br /> Because that's what you're saying even if it's not what you mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So since clarity was not what was needed I can only conclude that its use is one of spitefulness and </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> hypocrisy<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>If this is your only conclusion, than my previous point is that much less hyperbole and that much more an affirmation that my reading was accurate to your intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and to have a discussion on whether or not a correction should be made to the way we speak to each other. </div> </div> </div>Except it seems abundantly clear that you were never open to the &quot;correction&quot; being &quot;people that don't like nWW or similar terms realizing that it's not the problem and to stop calling people out for using it because that's far more divisive and disrespectful than using the term ever could be.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it has been pointed out WW is no more so it is somewhat a moot point, but unfortunately many still persist in using terminology that is now incorrect. </div> </div> </div>Well, WW isn't actually no more, it's no more as an independent entity. We don't know if Paradox will continue using the imprint or not. And again, &quot;terminology that is not incorrect&quot; is a sign that this was never really up for discussion. &quot;nWW&quot; was always going to be wrong and need correction to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So once again I can only conclude that its use is an attempt to marginalize or just be spiteful especially by continuing to use it. </div> </div> </div>Which is, again, a conclusion that can only stem from bad faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is not being used in many instances for clarification. </div> </div> </div>You realize it is, in most instances, being used for clarity so clarification later isn't necessary, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 11-17-2018, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T15:56:21-08:00","id":1268421,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> my intentions are not to police but to ask if it is really necessary to use. That's why I asked &quot;should we&quot; instead of stating that &quot;it should go&quot; I feel I have stated that clearly, but since you seemto think I am trying to police I can only conclude that I did not do a good job at that. As I have said I am checking myself but my conclusions color the way I feel, so I wanted clarity. But people seem to keep questioning the way I felt, so maybe I am just wrong in feeling that way.<br /> <br /> I am not going to go throughout the forums to point to the instances where it made me feelthat it was used in a negative form. You can do that yourself. I am taking the stance of what I felt and I don't need to prove my feelings for them to be valid. It is a fact that I felt that way and I asked to explain how the heck it made me feel that way and I was attempting to oblige.<br /> <br /> I do feel that such terminology has been used on occasion in a negative connotation. I don't think you use it as such and truly are just trying to be clear in your posts even if I feel it is unnecessary you do not and that is fine with me. But even you have been accessed of using it in a divisive manner which leads me to think that I am not the only one who feels the way I do about the use of the term. So I asked should we avoid using it? If you feel so, don't use it. If you don't feel so then you will continue to use it. If an individual is wanting to create a negative connotation then you have made me feel the negative stance you have taken, so well done. and those individuals will continue to use it but I can not police or control it, even if I wanted to which I don't.<br /> <br /> I would like people who may be using it in a negative manor to think about it before deciding to use it in the future, as some do feel like it is divisive or marginalizing and they don't need to prove their feelings either.<br /> <br /> on another note, I could really care less if people like V5 or not, so long as you are happy playing any edition of Vampire and that makes you happy and if not I am sorry you feel that way VtM is a good setting I hope you give it a try sometime. V5 is the edition I enjoy the most even though I have felt attack for licking it and I feel it is the best edition yet, but that is just my opinion and it is valid for me which is enough for me. What I do care about is when people spread lies about, oversimplify, or parrot other peoples statements with no real knowledge about the system when they are not true. If you have read the book and do not like it then that is your feelings on the matter and that is fine, but I feel you should state it as such so you don't confuse people on what is fact or you opinion.<br /> <br /> The conversation I had with Levi and the stances I took on WW printing the Chechen section has gotten me thinking on wether or not one should stand up when they feel marginalized even if it is about a work of fiction, and I am not equating these two incidents. I took the stance that &quot;Vampires aren't real&quot; but the ramifications that have been had over the work of fiction has made me rethink the matter all together. So I decided to voice my feelings on a separate issue I was having. I will not make that mistake again and with that I bow out of this altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 11-17-2018, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T06:52:53-08:00","id":1268536,"title":"","content":"I don't think you realise what being 'marginalised' is. It's not about hurt feelings. It's about power. <br /> <br /> See: <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marginalization\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marginalization</a><br /> <br /> People who are marginalised are disenfranchised, disempowered and discriminated against. Pointing to a brief, reductive definition in a dictionary doesn't get across the full depth of the concept and the context in which it exists.<br /> <br /> That said, the term nuWW in itself is no more loaded than other options. In fact, it's possibly less loaded than ParaWolf. The latter always reminds me of 'paramilitary'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T11:46:03-08:00","id":1268599,"title":"","content":"I don't see any reason to stop using 'NuWW.' The company is a distinct entity, different from the WW of old and OPP. That a lot of people use it disparagingly is just down to some people not liking the company. Asking us to not use it would be like not using 'TSR' because some people hated the company and called it T$R.<br /> <br /> It's also, quite frankly, a ridiculously unrealistic request. Only a tiny number of people are going to see this thread. Even if we were inclined to stop using the term, it wouldn't make a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T19:46:06-08:00","id":1269418,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve never cared for it. The fact is that there have been several White Wolfs over the years, as the same people were not consistently in charge, and the overall direction of products has changed a number of times with different people at the helm. It\u2019s just that whereas before White Wolf was more of a Theseus\u2019s Ship situation, under CCP it was dissolved as a company, so the recent White Wolf didn\u2019t have thstnsame continuity. Now it\u2019s also being dissolved, so... whatever. <br /> <br /> On the one hand, yeah, it was a different company with the same name, but White Wolf has been quite a number of companies over the years really, just with more obvious continuity between incarnations. And to be honest, \u201cNuWW\u201d seems to always be used in a negative tone, though I guess at this point it doesn\u2019t much matter. <br /> <br /> The situation from this point on is going to be a lot more like the CCP situation, only with less neglect, or so I expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T02:18:26-08:00","id":1269488,"title":"","content":"We could always try &quot;Chronicles of White Wolf.&quot;<br /> <br /> But seriously - NuWW as short for &quot;The new White Wolf&quot; to distinguish Paradox's rpg imprint from old White Wolf (CCP's rpg imprint) does not seem disparaging to me. When the difference doesn't matter, they're just White Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T10:03:47-08:00","id":1277217,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11720_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11720\" data-vbnamecard=\"11720\">Redwulfe</a> Without getting into the semantic weeds about whether you reasonably should feel/are marginalized by whatever distinction, I'm just going to point out that the emergence of the terminological distinctions is itself evidence of the community's desire to differentiate between certain items for rhetorical purposes--just like how people discuss different editions of the game, or comparisons between V:tM and V:tR, people in this fan community are going to talk about how the old and new stack up and compare with one another. Some of these conversations will make normative statements about quality and merit, some will simply discuss technical differences across the spectrum, and some will do both. Regardless, the conversations are going to happen.<br /> <br /> If some particular terminology is upsetting to you, and you'd like it not used, I suggest you first provide an alternative (because, again, these conversations are going to happen--it cannot be stopped); and, second, try to find a way to provide the community with a reasonable explanation as to why the particular term being used upsets you, beyond simply the fact that you don't like that people are going acknowledge that a difference exists between different production eras of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T11:32:35-08:00","id":1277234,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't we be moving onto ModWW now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T14:46:04-08:00","id":1277263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1277234#post1277234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't we be moving onto ModWW now?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's basically just Modiphius now. White Wolf is a branding used by Paradox for the IP and not much more. Modiphius and partners ( OPP and others) are in charge of game direction and production now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T15:06:30-08:00","id":1277267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1277263#post1277263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's basically just Modiphius now. White Wolf is a branding used by Paradox for the IP and not much more. Modiphius and partners ( OPP and others) are in charge of game direction and production now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right now that MOd is in charge shouldn't it be Mod WW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T17:18:42-08:00","id":1277284,"title":"","content":"That doesn't make any sense. It would be like saying we should be calling things OnyxWW. Modiphius isn't in charge of White Wolf. Modiphius is in charge of whatever IPs Paradox hires them to handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T19:30:48-08:00","id":1277295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1277284#post1277284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't make any sense. It would be like saying we should be calling things OnyxWW. Modiphius isn't in charge of White Wolf. Modiphius is in charge of whatever IPs Paradox hires them to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We call things Onyxpath I mean we could easily point out the &quot;Onyx Path&quot; period of White wolf games. Where they were the only ones doing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Modiphius isn't in charge of WW now.. but Paradox has functionally given up all its power as NuWW to Modiphius, going forward Modiphius will be running everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T19:38:26-08:00","id":1277296,"title":"","content":"Modiphius is in the same position as Onyx Path was under CCP. We can call it the Modiphius era if we want, but it's not ModWW because Modiphius isn't calling itself WW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T20:27:11-08:00","id":1277300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1268002-should-the-use-of-nuww-go?p=1277296#post1277296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Modiphius is in the same position as Onyx Path was under CCP. We can call it the Modiphius era if we want, but it's not ModWW because Modiphius isn't calling itself WW.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not sure that it is? It looks like Modiphius has complete Reign unlike OP which had to send in all its books for approval?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T00:01:55-08:00","id":1277311,"title":"","content":"However hands on/handsoff Paradox wants to handle oversight of Modiphius isn't really relevant is it?<br /> <br /> The point of calling it nWW or nuWW or whatever, was to clarify between different entities that used the same name. Modiphius, Paradox Interactive, and Onyx Path aren't also names of other companies we need to be clear which ones were talking about. WWGS and WWAB were two different corporate entities both using the name White Wolf. What's unclear here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}